---The data for an entity annotation. Represents a phrase in the conversation that is a known entity, such as a person, an organization, or location.
---@class gcp.contactcenterinsights_v1.GoogleCloudContactcenterinsightsV1Entity
---@field displayName? string The representative name for the entity.
---@field metadata? gcp.contactcenterinsights_v1.StringMap Metadata associated with the entity. For most entity types, the metadata is a Wikipedia URL (`wikipedia_url`) and Knowledge Graph MID (`mid`), if they are available. For the metadata associated with other entity types, see the Type table below.
---@field sentiment? gcp.contactcenterinsights_v1.GoogleCloudContactcenterinsightsV1SentimentData The aggregate sentiment expressed for this entity in the conversation.
---@field salience? number The salience score associated with the entity in the [0, 1.0] range. The salience score for an entity provides information about the importance or centrality of that entity to the entire document text. Scores closer to 0 are less salient, while scores closer to 1.0 are highly salient.
---@field type? gcp.contactcenterinsights_v1.GoogleCloudContactcenterinsightsV1EntityTypeEnum|string The entity type.

---@alias gcp.contactcenterinsights_v1.GoogleCloudContactcenterinsightsV1EntityMap { [string]: gcp.contactcenterinsights_v1.GoogleCloudContactcenterinsightsV1Entity }

